# known-miss.list — package names that fail apt-checks.sh because they live
# in repos the toolkit adds at install time (contrib/non-free) but which
# are NOT in the default Devuan Excalibur sources.list. Packages listed
# here are real, verified against the Devuan Excalibur archive — they are
# NOT typos. See: scripts/lib/common.sh (ensure_repo_component), 11-backports.sh.
#
# Format: one package name per line (lines starting with # are comments).
libdvd-pkg
winetricks
# codium: from VSCodium's own APT repo (download.vscodium.com), added by
# 40-vscodium.sh — never in the default Devuan Excalibur archive.
codium
# steam: lives in the contrib component, which only exists after
# scripts/lib/common.sh ensure_repo_component appends contrib/non-free at install time.
steam
# heroic: not an archive package at all. Heroic Games Launcher is fetched as a
# third-party .deb from its own GitHub release by 44-gaming.sh (it is not in
# contrib), and on this machine it is in fact installed as the Flatpak
# com.heroicgameslauncher.hgl. Nothing in Devuan Excalibur, contrib or
# non-free can ever satisfy it, so an apt-cache lookup would always miss.
heroic
